WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.580
Hey, welcome to Models and Agents for Beginners, Episode 78.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.000
It's June 20th, 2026.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.200
Today's AI news is pretty exciting, and I promise, no jargon.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:10.880
Let's go.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.280
Something wild just happened inside chat GPT

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.820
that could change how you use it every single day.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:21.420
Open AI added a new scheduled page where you can tell the chat

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.860
bot to run tasks at set times without you doing anything.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.000
Instead of typing the same question over and over,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.040
you set it once and the system checks on its own.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.720
Think of it like setting an alarm on your phone that only rings

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.740
if something important actually happens.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.460
The old pulse feature is being replaced, so this one page now handles

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.860
all your repeating requests in one spot.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.540
For a student, this could mean asking it to watch for new scholarship deadlines

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.820
and only text you when something changes.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.620
For someone who follows music or games, it means less time refreshing websites

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.900
and more time actually enjoying the hobby.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.860
The bigger shift is that chat GPT moves from a tool you have to open

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:06.000
yourself into something that works quietly in the background.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:09.460
If you have chat GPT plus, open the sidebar,

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.880
click the new scheduled page, and try setting one simple repeating task

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.260
like checking for new podcast episodes.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.760
The system will handle the rest and only send an alert

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.020
when it finds something new.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.760
Okay, now for my favorite part of the show,

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.360
the deep dive where we look under the hood.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:29.340
Today's concept is a multi-agent system,

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:34.800
which just means several different AIs working together like teammates on one project.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.020
Imagine you are doing a big group project at school where one person

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:41.680
gathers facts, another writes the report,

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.420
and a third checks everything for mistakes.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:49.480
That same idea happens here, except seven separate AIs each

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.760
handle one part of turning raw numbers into a finished story.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.900
One AI turns a plain spreadsheet into readable sentences.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.360
Another searches the web for extra facts to add.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.040
A third draws charts to make the numbers easier to see.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:09.560
A fourth checks every sentence and adds links so readers can verify the details themselves.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:14.400
The whole group keeps passing work back and forth until the final result is ready.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:18.920
In tests, 93% of the statements came with clickable sources

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.980
and many readers actually preferred the AI version.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.500
And that is basically how a multi-agent system works.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:26.740
Not so scary, right?

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.980
Now let's look at some cool stuff you can try right away.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.520
Apple's updated Siri now feels more like texting a helpful friend

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.160
than giving orders to a machine.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:40.720
It can stay in a conversation without forgetting what you said two turns ago.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:44.080
If you have an iPhone, hold the side button or say,

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:47.020
hey Siri, and try asking it to plan a simple route

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.320
or set a reminder for later in the day.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:53.800
Notice how it handles normal wording instead of requiring perfect commands.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:58.380
Next up, Norway is taking a thoughtful step with younger students.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:04.160
Starting late August, generative AI tools will not be allowed in grades one through seven,

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:07.760
so kids can master reading, writing, and math first.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:13.100
Secondary schools can still use the tools, but only with a teacher watching.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:17.500
The idea is to protect basic skills before shortcuts become the habit.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.980
Here are two quick bits worth knowing.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:26.580
A new report shows that 10% of people worldwide now check AI chat bots for news every week.

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.640
The figure rose from 7% the year before.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:33.540
Only 4% of users click through to the original source.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.940
Most people therefore receive summaries without seeing the full story.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:41.900
The data were published by the hyphendecoder.com.

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:46.120
The report tracks weekly use of chat bots for current events.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:50.800
Researchers built a benchmark that mimics actual knowledge work tasks.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:54.600
The best models could only fully solve 3% of them.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:59.220
The test focuses on messy real jobs rather than clean questions.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:04.180
A large gap remains between homework style performance and practical work.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.220
Details on the benchmark appeared on the decoder.com.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:13.540
The results measure how far current systems still fall short on complex assignments.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:19.620
That's it for today. Remember, every AI expert started exactly where you are right now.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:23.380
If something we talked about today made you curious, go try it.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:25.160
That's literally how learning works.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.120
Stay curious, keep experimenting, and we'll see you tomorrow.

